# SkyPane -- production env template.
#
# Copy this file to `deploy/skypane.env` ON THE VPS ONLY (never in this
# repo, never on a laptop) and fill in the real values there. `skypane.env`
# must NEVER be committed, and its contents must NEVER be pasted into a
# build log, an issue, or a chat transcript — same discipline as
# `firmware/main/secrets.example.h` (see that file for the pattern this one
# mirrors). systemd reads this file as root via `EnvironmentFile=` — before
# any unit drops privileges to its own `User=` — in every SkyPane unit
# (`skypane-poll`, `skypane-byos`, `skypane-companion`); no python-dotenv
# or other loader library is involved.
# table). Because systemd is the only reader, `deploy/provision.sh` makes
# the real file on the VPS `root:root 0600` -- no service
# process reads it directly as the `skypane` user, confirmed by grepping
# every `os.environ` read in this codebase before that decision was made.

# Device enrolment no longer uses a shared secret in this file. Each frame
# has its own enrolment secret, provisioned into its flash and registered on
# this VPS as a SHA-256 hash only — see deploy/README.md's "Device
# enrolment (per-device secret)" section. The registry lives at
# ${SKYPANE_STATE_DIR}/devices.json and is managed with
# stub-server/devices_cli.py; there is nothing to fill in here for it. If a
# real skypane.env on this VPS still carries a line reading
# SKYPANE_BYOS_SECRET=..., that line is harmless (byos_server.py no longer
# reads it) and can be deleted.

# The loopback port byos_server.py listens on. Caddy reverse-proxies to
# this port; nothing else should ever reach it directly (ufw denies the
# app port from outside — see deploy/provision.sh).
SKYPANE_BYOS_PORT=8642

# Fallback sleep_s handed to the frame in every /device/v1/display
# response — how long the device sleeps between polls. This is now only
# the fallback (11-web-configurable-wake-interval): once a value is set
# on the companion Settings page's Wake interval field, that per-device
# on-disk value overrides this one, taking effect on the device's next
# poll with no service restart needed. The companion process also reads
# this same variable to pre-fill that field on first load — but only
# when the value is within the field's own 60-3600s bounds, so the
# shipped 30 below renders the field's placeholder instead of a number.
SKYPANE_SLEEP_S=30

# Directory holding panel.bin / poll_state.json / enrichment cache on the
# VPS. Both skypane-poll.service and skypane-byos.service must agree on
# this path — a mismatch here serves a stale or missing panel forever
# (see this plan's key_links warning).
SKYPANE_STATE_DIR=/opt/skypane/state

# The public hostname the device is configured to reach, e.g. a
# <dashed-vps-ip>.nip.io hostname (deploy/Caddyfile) or a real owned
# domain later. Used only for operator convenience (deploy.sh's log
# printing, README verification commands) — Caddy itself reads the
# hostname from deploy/Caddyfile, not from this file.
SKYPANE_PUBLIC_HOST=203-0-113-10.nip.io

# The companion configuration web interface's shared password
# -- there are no per-user accounts, this single value is the only access
# control on that interface). Generate a real value yourself, e.g.:
# openssl rand -hex 32 — a 32-byte random value, the same length discipline
# as every device enrolment secret. Same never-committed discipline: this
# file carries a placeholder only, the real value is written by hand on the
# VPS, in deploy/skypane.env, never in this repo.
SKYPANE_COMPANION_PASSWORD=replace-with-a-long-random-secret

# The loopback port companion/app.py listens on. Caddy reverse-proxies to
# this port and ufw denies it from outside — exactly as SKYPANE_BYOS_PORT
# above is treated.
SKYPANE_COMPANION_PORT=8643

# The companion interface's public hostname: config-<public-host> by
# default (e.g. config-<dashed-vps-ip>.nip.io), or its own domain
# passed as provision.sh's second argument (production:
# skypane.algernon.ovh since 2026-09-23) — distinct from
# SKYPANE_PUBLIC_HOST above so the two services have separate names and
# separate TLS certificates. Used only for operator convenience, same as
# SKYPANE_PUBLIC_HOST; Caddy itself reads the real hostname from
# deploy/Caddyfile.
SKYPANE_COMPANION_HOST=config-203-0-113-10.nip.io

# Drop the Secure flag on the companion's cookies (session + UI theme).
# NEVER set this in production — it lets the session cookie travel over
# cleartext, which is exactly the offline-sniffing exposure the Secure
# flag exists to prevent. This exists ONLY for a plain-http LAN or dev
# run (no Caddy/TLS in front), where an unconditional Secure flag made
# the login round-trip silently unwinnable (a browser never sends a
# Secure cookie back over plain http). Fails closed: the ONLY value
# that drops Secure is exactly `1` — "true", "yes", or any other value
# leaves Secure on. Commented out below; leave it that way in
# deploy/skypane.env on the VPS.
# SKYPANE_COMPANION_INSECURE_COOKIES=1

# Durable path to Caddy's structured JSON access log for the
# device-protocol site block. This is the file the companion service
# tails for the device's battery telemetry (X-Battery-Mv) — the only path
# to that data, since the vendored stub-server/byos_server.py prints the
# header and persists nothing, and must not be modified.
SKYPANE_CADDY_ACCESS_LOG=/opt/skypane/state/caddy-access.log

# Path to the off-box backup freshness marker. Written by
# deploy/backup/backup_gate.py's `ack` verb on every successful pull the
# Mac's launchd agent makes (deploy/backup/mac/skypane-backup-pull.sh) —
# never by the companion itself. Read by the companion's Health page,
# which shows "last off-box backup N ago" and turns into a warning once
# the named archive's own snapshot timestamp is older than 3 days, or
# when the marker is missing or unreadable. Leaving this unset (the
# default in development, tests, and Playwright) simply hides that line —
# it is not an error condition on its own.
SKYPANE_OFFBOX_MARKER=/var/lib/skypane-backup/pulled/last-pull
